{
  "id": "low1.L23",
  "paper": "low-energy-phenomenology",
  "selection_status": "selected",
  "statement": "The repaired owner binds ordinaryFull in raw action units: ordinaryFull = (h_source*c_source)*beta*input.normalizedAmplitude = beta*input.amplitude, where beta is the source photon-left-reader of the same prepared covector. Keeping the original full-light/contact equation ordinaryFull-lightResponse=sourceCEM+contactResponse, the single (h_source*c_source)^-1 readout equals sourceCEM/(h_source*c_source). Conversion to the earlier matching consumer preserves the same values and equation; the full-light return consumes this owner.",
  "quantifiers_premises": [
    "ordinaryFull, lightResponse, contactResponse and sourceCEM share raw action units; the readout applies (h_source*c_source)^-1 once.",
    "ordinaryFull-lightResponse=sourceCEM+contactResponse is a supplied condition; lightResponse and contactResponse are matching-owner values.",
    "The input is the nativeY-prepared photon amplitude, not the actual edge-0 electron; existing 17-companion Riesz/six-test obligations retain their identities.",
    "No new physical transverse carrier, zero-transfer/Thomson/alpha(0) matching."
  ],
